<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICA KWV WINE CO-OP BITTER ABOUT WINE TAX HIKE.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICA KWV WINE CO-OP BITTER ABOUT WINE TAX HIKE.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's KWV wine and brandy co-operative on Thursday criticised wine tax increases in the budget, saying this could result in a drop in sales and an increase in smuggling.</p>
<p>&quot;These increases appear out of place,&quot; it said in a statement. &quot;A situation of diminishing returns is facing the industry and the state.&quot;</p>
<p>It said &quot;tax shocks&quot; like that in the budget on Wednesday would aggravate smuggling and illegal trading.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 252-238</p>
</text>
